<title>SINGAPORE: India awards July Bombay LAN to Glencore - traders.</title>
<headline>India awards July Bombay LAN to Glencore - traders.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded to Swiss trader Glencore a tender to sell 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) at $33.75 per tonne discount to spot U.S. Gulf 87 octane gasoline quotes on a free-on-board Bombay July 20-22 lifting, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closed on July 10 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN tender from Bombay for June 17-19 lifting was awarded at a $16.00 per tonne discount to Japanese spot quotes on a fob basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3093)</p>
